192
00:24:54,871 --> 00:25:01,819
I have no teacher and one like me exists nowhere in the world with all his gods because I have no person as my counterpart.

193
00:25:02,500 --> 00:25:04,262
I am the accomplished one in the world.

194
00:25:04,563 --> 00:25:06,266
I am the teacher supreme.

195
00:25:06,486 --> 00:25:08,067
I alone am fully enlightened.

196
00:25:08,317 --> 00:25:10,820
whose fires are quenched and extinguished.

197
00:25:12,102 --> 00:25:18,788
Now, when Upaka hears this, he says, by your claims, friend, you ought to be the universal victor.

198
00:25:19,670 --> 00:25:24,335
And the Buddha replies, the victors are those like me who have won the destruction of the taints.

199
00:25:24,875 --> 00:25:26,416
Remember the taints, the oozings.

200
00:25:27,538 --> 00:25:32,182
I have vanquished all evil states, therefore, Upaka, I am a victor.

201
00:25:33,144 --> 00:25:37,448
Now, the Ajivaka Upaka, when has said this,

202
00:25:37,833 --> 00:25:44,483
He said, maybe so, friend, shaking his head, he took a bypass and departed.

203
00:25:44,785 --> 00:25:50,474
So he wasn't particularly impressed by the Buddha's declaration of enlightenment.

204
00:25:51,175 --> 00:25:57,006
I think it might have been a teaching point for the Buddha, really.

205
00:25:58,116 --> 00:26:16,155
Anyway, from then on, we've mentioned this before, he goes to see his five companions and then spends the whole of his life traversing the north part of India, teaching all the way from Delhi, all the way across that northern part.

206
00:26:16,375 --> 00:26:19,138
His whole life is just devoted to that.

207
00:26:20,941 --> 00:26:27,988
So we can end our little passage here with this lovely setting for his

208
00:26:28,255 --> 00:26:52,946
departure for his what's called parinibbana so when when a person achieves um achieves arahatship when when they they still have this body they still have this mind which has traces of their old habits but when they die of course all that's away and therefore it's called parinibbana full total nibbana

209
00:26:54,479 --> 00:27:09,011
So the Buddha's been poisoned, not purposefully, by Channa, who has given him some, they think it's either truffles, what pigs eat, or some...

210
00:27:09,700 --> 00:27:13,545
some pork truffles.

211
00:27:14,425 --> 00:27:20,634
I think I've only had it once and I can't say I've talked to them immediately, but they're supposed to be a very great delicacy.

212
00:27:21,275 --> 00:27:31,868
For those of you who haven't, it's slightly garlicky, deep dusky aroma, earthy, pungent, that's what I remember, and funky, I call it.

213
00:27:31,888 --> 00:27:37,817
They're not, they're not, they're a fungus, but they're not mushrooms because they don't live over the ground.

214
00:27:38,387 --> 00:27:42,252
So he could have been eating truffles.

215
00:27:43,054 --> 00:27:45,057
Frankly, I can't imagine it personally.

216
00:27:45,396 --> 00:27:48,922
It would be more pork, which goes off very quickly, as you know.

217
00:27:50,644 --> 00:27:51,545
So he's dying.

218
00:27:51,605 --> 00:27:54,509
He's dying from this gastroenteritis.

219
00:27:54,848 --> 00:27:56,551
And he's an old man.

220
00:27:56,612 --> 00:27:57,252
He's 80.

221
00:27:57,712 --> 00:27:59,295
And he's lying there.

222
00:28:00,115 --> 00:28:02,199
And his life's ebbing away.

223
00:28:02,680 --> 00:28:03,359
And here he is.

224
00:28:03,461 --> 00:28:05,323
He's still teaching.

225
00:28:06,046 --> 00:28:18,438
Then the Lord addressed the monks, saying, it may be, monk, that some monks have doubts and uncertainty about the Buddha, the Dharma, the Sangha, or about the path or the practice.

226
00:28:19,419 --> 00:28:27,646
Ask me now, monks, do not afterwards feel remorse, thinking the teacher was there before us and we failed to ask the Lord face to face.

227
00:28:28,827 --> 00:28:34,534
At these words, the monks were silent and the Lord repeated his words a second and third time.

228
00:28:35,087 --> 00:28:36,910
And still the monks were silent.

229
00:28:37,569 --> 00:28:42,494
Then he said, perhaps you do not ask out of respect for the teacher.

230
00:28:43,296 --> 00:28:46,838
Then let one friend tell it to another.

231
00:28:47,440 --> 00:28:48,800
But still they were silent.

232
00:28:49,862 --> 00:28:55,107
Ananda said, oh, it's wonderful how there are no doubts and uncertainty.

233
00:28:55,948 --> 00:29:02,714
And the Buddha replies, indeed, I don't see anybody here who has less attained than a stream entrance.

234
00:29:03,826 --> 00:29:06,391
one who's got the first of the attainments.

235
00:29:07,452 --> 00:29:17,310
And then we have this lovely ending where the Buddha says to him, I declare all conditioned things are of a nature to decay.

236
00:29:17,631 --> 00:29:21,258
Strive diligently for your liberation.

237
00:29:21,278 --> 00:29:22,460
And he passes away.

238
00:29:22,519 --> 00:29:24,483
And that was it.

239
00:29:26,859 --> 00:29:36,609
And those monks who had not yet overcome their passions, wept and tore their hair, raising their arms, throwing themselves down and twisting and turning, crying.

240
00:29:36,849 --> 00:29:39,373
All too soon, the blessed one has passed away.

241
00:29:40,133 --> 00:29:42,536
All too soon, the welfare has passed away.

242
00:29:43,115 --> 00:29:45,919
All too soon, the eye of the world has disappeared.

243
00:29:48,741 --> 00:29:52,065
I actually saw this also with an elderly monk who died.

244
00:29:52,144 --> 00:29:55,669
It was a beloved teacher in Sri Lanka and

245
00:29:56,070 --> 00:29:59,115
The young monks couldn't stop themselves from crying.

246
00:29:59,555 --> 00:30:02,798
They had that relationship of son to father.

247
00:30:04,040 --> 00:30:07,084
And then, of course, there's always those who have gone beyond.

248
00:30:07,144 --> 00:30:19,799
And so the Venerable Araruda, whom we've met before, who's very good at explaining the Dharma, friends, enough of your weeping and wailing.

249
00:30:20,134 --> 00:30:28,487
Has not the Lord already told you that all things that are pleasant and delightful are changeable, subject to separation and becoming other?

250
00:30:28,907 --> 00:30:30,450
So that put a damper on it, didn't it?

251
00:30:33,153 --> 00:30:35,057
So we have to leave it there.

252
00:30:35,897 --> 00:30:44,329
His remains are split into eight parts for the different tribes or clans who wanted it.

253
00:30:44,770 --> 00:30:49,196
And today, of course, there's a great big stupor that he longs

254
00:30:49,446 --> 00:30:54,515
Yes, a big stupa at Kusinagara where he died.

255
00:30:54,555 --> 00:30:59,721
And so that brings us to the end of the Buddha's life.

256
00:31:01,084 --> 00:31:02,246
It's good to read about it.

257
00:31:02,306 --> 00:31:09,497
There are many biographies, some of them follow the more imaginative

258
00:31:09,815 --> 00:31:12,258
story and some are very basic.

259
00:31:12,817 --> 00:31:25,933
As you know, in parts of the scriptures, they say his father was like a king and he had three gardens, one for the rainy season, the dry season and the cold season.

260
00:31:26,694 --> 00:31:31,019
But basically, he was just an aristocrat.

261
00:31:31,759 --> 00:31:33,982
His father was the head of a group.

262
00:31:34,434 --> 00:31:40,942
of a clan who had to pay tribute to the local king, Pasenadi of Kosala.

263
00:31:42,584 --> 00:31:46,127
So reading the Buddha's story is an inspiration for us.

264
00:31:46,528 --> 00:31:50,232
We're only going through what he went through, a life of renunciation.

265
00:31:50,594 --> 00:31:58,241
And in the end, without any doubt, we will all be fully liberated, hopefully sooner rather than later.

266
00:32:00,204 --> 00:32:01,506
So we can do a bit of practice.

